{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta","id":773235,"title":"The best-worst 1st ed messes in WtA","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-24T10:21:36-08:00","id":773235,"title":"The best-worst 1st ed messes in WtA","content":"The first editions of each WoD game are important. They started these games and got people interested in the games in the first place.<br /> <br /> However, they also included a lot of silly, igmorant or just baffling stuff, due to when they were made and tone they were going for.<br /> <br /> Here's my list;<br /> <br /> - Get of Fenris, the nazi tribe. This freaking thing became basically a burr on the tribe like no other. You can still find players to this day that fully thing this was what the tribe was about.<br /> <br /> -The White Howlers being taken pretty much from Rober E. Howard's Worms of the Earth by concept.<br /> <br /> - Bunyip, just, Bunyip. Shattered Dreams has done wonders fixing them, thankfully. But the base concept was literally taking a wolf-like creature as their specie, making them peaceful compared to other garou and defined because how they died and pretty much nothing else.<br /> <br /> -The 1st ed Silent Strider tribebook's Serial Killer template. If you ever have a chance, just look how badly it would work with -anything-.<br /> <br /> -The 1st ed Fenrir tribebook's Ahroun template seriously made me burst in laughter as I saw it. It is so stereotypical and macho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T10:58:43-08:00","id":773252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta#post773235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Bunyip, just, Bunyip. Shattered Dreams has done wonders fixing them, thankfully. But the base concept was literally taking a wolf-like creature as their specie, making them peaceful compared to other garou and defined because how they died and pretty much nothing else..</div> </div> </div> </div>This concurs with many of my thoughts. I'd like to think I've built a better framework for the Bunyip that has guided writers to improving much of what came before. Hopefully when we get to expand the Shattered Dreams ideas into Tribebook: Bunyip we'll be able to explore these ideas in more detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T11:27:40-08:00","id":773273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=773252#post773252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This concurs with many of my thoughts. I'd like to think I've built a better framework for the Bunyip that has guided writers to improving much of what came before. Hopefully when we get to expand the Shattered Dreams ideas into Tribebook: Bunyip we'll be able to explore these ideas in more detail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, just by addressing the marsupial in the room, you've done good work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T11:32:04-08:00","id":773277,"title":"","content":"Tribe book Bunyip brings a smile to my face.<br /> <br /> The Silver Fangs as inbred royalist plagued by insanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T13:20:56-08:00","id":773371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta#post773235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The White Howlers being taken pretty much from Rober E. Howard's Worms of the Earth by concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like a lot of the Howardiana in early WoD. I think there are a lot of good things that can be mined from that. Descendants of the Lost Picts isn't a bad idea (although I think it better if they are the descendants of the original European peoples before the Indo-European migrations, and the Picts were just the last outpost of that). Most of the laughable ideas about the Black Spiral Dancers are not directly developed from that idea.<br /> <br /> I don't mind the idea of marsupial were-creatures, and the Thylacine are interesting. Garou slaughtering an ally because they are ignorant, macho jerks is a strong idea. I don't like the idea that they are &quot;Garou&quot;. It works better if the Bunyip are another Changing Breed. If you truly need an actual Garou tribe that was killed by the other Garou, the designers should have found another way to accomplish that in the setting. In my chronicles, I don't have the Bunyip be Garou and it has absolutely zero negative effect.<br /> <br /> Many of the First Edition tribe books are laughable and contained many bad ideas. There are many good ideas as well. It's just that the writers only had so much time to develop their ideas without considering how well they would hold up. It is just a shame that the desire to keep continuity meant everything has to be retained to some degree.<br /> <br /> The biggest knock on 1st edition is probably that the writers took what were relevant modern topics of the time and made them essential things about the Tribe, forgetting that these topics would mean nothing to the Tribe for thousands of years in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T13:35:01-08:00","id":773382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=773371#post773371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually like a lot of the Howardiana in early WoD. I think there are a lot of good things that can be mined from that. Descendants of the Lost Picts isn't a bad idea (although I think it better if they are the descendants of the original European peoples before the Indo-European migrations, and the Picts were just the last outpost of that). Most of the laughable ideas about the Black Spiral Dancers are not directly developed from that idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I just didn't know this and so was disappointed when I found out. The idea of picts being from another fantasy book, rather than mythology or actual history annoyed me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=773371#post773371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest knock on 1st edition is probably that the writers took what were relevant modern topics of the time and made them essential things about the Tribe, forgetting that these topics would mean nothing to the Tribe for thousands of years in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I forgot to mention the Child of Gaia being based on white middle class hippies very strongly XD<br /> <br /> Though, I've heard the Uktena were meant to be more Voodoo-Wolves than anything they later became. That sounded interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 11-24-2015, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T14:53:10-08:00","id":773445,"title":"","content":"The name of the metis breed. Yes, most of us know that it can work with the Greek titaness, but one the old Silver Fang tribebook's template tried to use a turn of phrase with it that ruined it forever. Now, I think we should take cues from the Kitsune and Nagah for naming them differently for everyone.<br /> <br /> Wolf-headed bikini babes in the artwork. Someone had to say it...<br /> <br /> Edit: Silver Fangs being focused so heavily on Russia, and the Stargazers being The (inscrutable and wise with kung fu) Asian Tribe. I want time for the House of the Blood Red Crest so that both can start to exit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta#post773235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -The 1st ed Silent Strider tribebook's Serial Killer template. If you ever have a chance, just look how badly it would work with -anything-.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There was a vigilante Philodox and a Theurge that was from the Addams family with some Lovecraftian tidbits, but no serial killer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 11-24-2015, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T15:05:55-08:00","id":773454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=773445#post773445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The name of the metis breed. Yes, most of us know that it can work with the Greek titaness, but one the old Silver Fang tribebook's template tried to use a turn of phrase with it that ruined it forever. Now, I think we should take cues from the Kitsune and Nagah for naming them differently for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? Seeing as I only got into cWoD after V20 was released I'm now wondering what the tribebook could have done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: Silver Fangs being focused so heavily on Russia, and the Stargazers being The (inscrutable and wise with kung fu) Asian Tribe. I want time for the House of the Blood Red Crest so that both can start to exit. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this annoys me. When I finally get W20 and run a game (I'm on a student budget) I plan to at least remove the Stargazers (and, for my first Chronicle, the Native American Tribes, I'll be focusing on the Europeans because I live right next door, but according to y government not in it), although I'm not sure what I'd do for the Silver Fangs, possibly make them the Germanic tribe? (The Holy Roman Empire was their attempt to unite all of Europe under one banner! I should also research more history before deciding stuff like this!). If I ever run an 'American', 'Asian', or 'African' Chronicle I plan to assemble a Tribes list for them (or just use the 3 official ones for Native Americans) based around their cultures and use the European tribes to assemble gift lists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T15:42:01-08:00","id":773474,"title":"","content":"Actually a Book of Silver Fang Houses would be nice. Developing Wise Heart in the Middle East Southern Europe, Blood Red Crest in India, and the &quot;Lost houses&quot;. I kinda was hoping for information on the House lost during the War of Rage in Shattered Dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T15:50:29-08:00","id":773481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=773445#post773445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolf-headed bikini babes in the artwork. Someone had to say it...</div> </div> </div> </div>I was perfectly fine with this part, if the art were actually good and not...well...fugly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T16:15:04-08:00","id":773493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=773454#post773454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, what? Seeing as I only got into cWoD after V20 was released I'm now wondering what the tribebook could have done.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the Ice Dancer, &quot;Your father was a Vietnamese-Canadian Stargazer; your mother, a French-Canadian Fang Philodox, making you metis in both senses of the word.&quot;<br /> <br /> MULTIKILL!. Let us count the failure points.<br /> <br /> 1 - first off, metis was supposed to be Metis, a reference to the Greek mythological titaness, pronounced mee-tees (like saying the English words me teas).<br /> 2 - she doesn't actually seem to be part First Nations, so not a metis with an accent pronounced may tea.<br /> 3 - Her house is historically from Asia, but her father, who was ethnically Vietnamese, was a Stargazer, and her mother, the Silver Fang, was, from the sound of it, wholly European. Sure, she could be from a line that got exchanged, but it strikes me as a tad too circuitous.<br /> <br /> Everything about that makes me glad that we aren't getting supplements treadmilled out anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, this annoys me. When I finally get W20 and run a game (I'm on a student budget) I plan to at least remove the Stargazers (and, for my first Chronicle, the Native American Tribes, I'll be focusing on the Europeans because I live right next door, but according to y government not in it), although I'm not sure what I'd do for the Silver Fangs, possibly make them the Germanic tribe? (The Holy Roman Empire was their attempt to unite all of Europe under one banner! I should also research more history before deciding stuff like this!). If I ever run an 'American', 'Asian', or 'African' Chronicle I plan to assemble a Tribes list for them (or just use the 3 official ones for Native Americans) based around their cultures and use the European tribes to assemble gift lists. </div> </div> </div>And the odd thing about Rage Across Russia was that it arguably made all of the non-Fianna tribes much more inclusive and expansive, or at least teetered on the edge of it. We got Siberian Uktena and Wendigo, we had Garou of most tribes that were Russian rather than the stereotypical ethnicities ascribed to them. Downside: the Fangs can't tell that Nicolai Predatelski is a turncoat. The guy who named himself &quot;Nick Backstabber&quot; in his own language. He's going about as a secret Wyrm agent. Ha ha ha ha ha ha... ha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 11-24-2015, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T17:53:10-08:00","id":773541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=773445#post773445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There was a vigilante Philodox and a Theurge that was from the Addams family with some Lovecraftian tidbits, but no serial killer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops, it was the theurge. It just left me baffled how to use it in a game at all, nevermind as a strider XD<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=773493#post773493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the odd thing about Rage Across Russia was that it arguably made all of the non-Fianna tribes much more inclusive and expansive, or at least teetered on the edge of it. We got Siberian Uktena and Wendigo, we had Garou of most tribes that were Russian rather than the stereotypical ethnicities ascribed to them. Downside: the Fangs can't tell that Nicolai Predatelski is a turncoat. The guy who named himself &quot;Nick Backstabber&quot; in his own language. He's going about as a secret Wyrm agent. Ha ha ha ha ha ha... ha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, obviously they wouldn't, they all spoke english after all. No way a russian would pick the game, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T19:23:02-08:00","id":773583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=773445#post773445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver Fangs being focused so heavily on Russia, and the Stargazers being The (inscrutable and wise with kung fu) Asian Tribe. I want time for the House of the Blood Red Crest so that both can start to exit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is so easy to eliminate both and keep the major concept of the tribe. I find myself doing a lot of canon edits like this for my own chronicle. I keep what I like and get rid of what I don't. Ironically, it is one reason I like First Edition - the subsequent editions keep building on the edifice of these concepts so it is harder to pull out interesting nuggets that aren't polluted. Everything is so fresh in First Edition, it is much easier to ignore what you don't like.<br /> <br /> Yes, northern Eurasia is the homeland of the Silver Fangs, but the presence of so many royal houses allows you to easily undermine the Russian dominance. Also, since the expansion of the Great Russians comes relatively late (for a game whose timeline goes back to the Ice Age), you can ignore even that. In my chronicle, the eldest and Purest Breed Silver Fangs in Russia come from the Samoyedic and Finno-Ugric peoples.<br /> <br /> Stargazers are also easy to reposition. Their role is simply to be the Garou philosophers. Nothing makes that particularly Asian. I keep their tribal homeland in the Himalayas, but they are found pretty much anywhere there are high mountains they can hunt in and get a good look at the night sky. And I have lots of other Garou in East Asia - the Shadow Lords among the Mongolian peoples, Korea, and Japan. Silver Fangs of Blood Red Crest in Central Asia and the Tarim Basin. Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers in the cities. Pretty much everything is there except the Pure Ones, Fianna, and Get of Fenris. Also, if you want to Kalindo, take Melee and then specialize.<br /> <br /> Sometimes White Wolf was incredibly racist in the way only well-meaning, but arrogant, liberals can be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T19:43:39-08:00","id":773599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=773583#post773583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stargazers are also easy to reposition. Their role is simply to be the Garou philosophers. Nothing makes that particularly Asian. I keep their tribal homeland in the Himalayas, but they are found pretty much anywhere there are high mountains they can hunt in and get a good look at the night sky. And I have lots of other Garou in East Asia - the Shadow Lords among the Mongolian peoples, Korea, and Japan. Silver Fangs of Blood Red Crest in Central Asia and the Tarim Basin. Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers in the cities. Pretty much everything is there except the Pure Ones, Fianna, and Get of Fenris. Also, if you want to Kalindo, take Melee and then specialize.<br /> <br /> Sometimes White Wolf was incredibly racist in the way only well-meaning, but arrogant, liberals can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it makes no sense for Gazers to be exclusively Asian. They are meant to be voices of reason, so why are they holed up so far from the rest?<br /> <br /> That, and I've always headcanoned that Shadow Lord have three branches they come from. The Slavic, the Iberian and the Asian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T22:59:40-08:00","id":773670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=773599#post773599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, and I've always headcanoned that Shadow Lord have three branches they come from. The Slavic, the Iberian and the Asian.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can easily reconcile the Asian and the Slavic since the Eurasian steppe connects many peoples together, but I've never understood how the Shadow Lords can be in Iberia except that the developers wanted them to be (since the SL are in many ways &quot;the Lasombra&quot; of the Garou, and the Lasombra vampire clan have ties to Spain).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T11:07:59-08:00","id":774136,"title":"","content":"At this point, I'd also heap a lot of &quot;the Black Furies are from Greece&quot; onto the fire as well, on account of how they're inspired by legends that the Greeks told about very much non-Greek people neighboring on Greek territory..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T11:38:27-08:00","id":774157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=774136#post774136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point, I'd also heap a lot of &quot;the Black Furies are from Greece&quot; onto the fire as well, on account of how they're inspired by legends that the Greeks told about very much non-Greek people neighboring on Greek territory..</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, any tribal concept that wasn't Glass Walker or Red Talons (and Bone Gnawers outside the omega tribe), AND was tied to a cultural thing, ended up being like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T01:16:45-08:00","id":774609,"title":"","content":"I'm fascinated with how from all the bad stereotypes early Werewolf made we got the tribes we got by Revised. The change was quite impressive. The Children of Gaia, the Black Furies and the Bone Gnawers still need some work, but at least they can be adapted into something useful if you work back to basics and add a liberal amount of mythology and history to them. The Silver Fangs being made cosmopolitan and tied to both nobility and influence was a great change.<br /> <br /> The Shadow Lords (even in Revised) are a bit iffy due to the fact that I don't really believe they ever actually bothered to properly research southeastern europe and Balcan history (even come Revised). Not as bad as some of the others, but they are not tied to any cultural group there and they really aren't properly using the history of war, religion and invasion. Heck one would think that the premier faction of Werewolves that has spent the ages on the bulwark of Europe would have a outlook on life defined by the area they come from, not by random one-upmanship. I'm also kinda curious how they manage the human conflicts between their different constituent cultures and their own Septs.<br /> <br /> Mind you, In the Balcans it's pretty normal to be celebrating, fucking and drinking with each other the one day and the cutting each other's throat the next, and then going back to what it was before.<br /> <br /> The Wyrm in 1st edition is pure comedy. Pentex is a hillarious two note villian and fomori are cannon fodder. It's fascinating how much deeper and scarier they got along the way.<br /> <br /> The Wyld as &quot;good&quot; and Werewolves as its &quot;protectors&quot;. Seriously, the whole triat got so much better once they became unfathomable cosmic forces that you cannot really relate to.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T13:10:58-08:00","id":776167,"title":"","content":"The level of racism in cWoD, specialy (but not only) in the 1st editions is astounding. They barely show any real knowledge of how the world is outside the United States. Seriously, I simply can't recognize my own country in their books, it seems like a fantasy otherworld instead (I'm from Brazil).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=774609#post774609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, the whole triat got so much better once they became unfathomable cosmic forces that you cannot really relate to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Suddenly I got inspired. What about making the Triat true lovecraftian outergods that both werewolves and their foes don't really comprehend, and work a chronicle on this premise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T15:06:07-08:00","id":776224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=776167#post776167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The level of racism in cWoD, specialy (but not only) in the 1st editions is astounding. They barely show any real knowledge of how the world is outside the United States. Seriously, I simply can't recognize my own country in their books, it seems like a fantasy otherworld instead (I'm from Brazil).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as far as Brazil was considered, it might as well been a fantasy world for the writers. Possibly all of it jungle.<br /> <br /> One thing that persisted to Revised, was the whole &quot;America is a garou dreamland&quot; thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T17:13:43-08:00","id":776288,"title":"","content":"At least in our Euro-centric culture you can say that Brasil is exotic and that it's harder to research then Europe (especially in a world without wikipedia and internet for everyone). Yet Europe is utterly and completley missed in all the early books. Even the later ones don't really understand the context they are writing about. But at least they're not as factually wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T17:37:24-08:00","id":776303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=776288#post776288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least in our Euro-centric culture you can say that Brasil is exotic and that it's harder to research then Europe (especially in a world without wikipedia and internet for everyone). Yet Europe is utterly and completley missed in all the early books. Even the later ones don't really understand the context they are writing about. But at least they're not as factually wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, just going by werewolf, Europe is the Old World. It seems small compared to America, it has lots of REALLY old cities. Therefore, it must be throughly Wyrm and Weaver tainted. It's the same easy darkness trope that made the Bunyip such a sad mess. And in a lot of revised books, especially Bone Gnawers and Children of Gaia (it's an example still, shut up), Europe is treated as a place the tribes left behind. In a lot of ways, pre-20th oWoD portrayed Europe as a place where time stood still, where old ways still stuck, compared to the free and open America.<br /> <br /> This actually lead to an interesting thing in my gaming. A couple of players spoke of their american Fenrir born characters learning danish and swedish in the home septs. And my first thought was 'why? You aren't from there, you are American'. Which I think also illustrates the difference in thought. To those players, they were upholding a culture. To me, it seemed strange and unneeded. Granted, I was in the wrong there in my thoughts. XD<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:26:22-08:00","id":776346,"title":"","content":"It wasn't that hard to do proper research back in the early-mid 90s, although the internet made it much easier in the late 90s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T19:25:50-08:00","id":776370,"title":"","content":"I'm going to nominate the tie in novels. A few actually reflected the source material, but a lot of it was just out there. (The Uktena summoning Fenris to tell the Get of Fenris that a woman is an Ahroun, and the Get <i>not accepting it</i>.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T20:46:30-08:00","id":776407,"title":"","content":"Werewolf Anthology had a story with Sam Haight, buying a clone body, discovering he had a son, who was a white howler.<br /> <br /> That story carried over into the book Hellstorm. Where Sammy recovers from his adventures as super twink, seeking out his son who is now friends with a ronin BSD and a n Assamite Antritribu (Joe Boot) fighting a massive wyrm dritter..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T20:52:12-08:00","id":776409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=776370#post776370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to nominate the tie in novels. A few actually reflected the source material, but a lot of it was just out there. (The Uktena summoning Fenris to tell the Get of Fenris that a woman is an Ahroun, and the Get <i>not accepting it</i>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>And the worst part? THIS is what people apparently remember about the game clearly. This, along with the mixed-heritage flaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T22:26:07-08:00","id":776429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=776409#post776409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the worst part? THIS is what people apparently remember about the game clearly. This, along with the mixed-heritage flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sometimes the horrible stuff is easy to remember.\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T23:52:23-08:00","id":776463,"title":"","content":"Oh, now that it's coming back to me, how could I forget the &quot;Garou gene&quot; of pre-Revised Werewolf? And some people even still refer to it as a thing...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=776409#post776409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the worst part? THIS is what people apparently remember about the game clearly. This, along with the mixed-heritage flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an extra-frustrating version of that stemming from fans of other classic WoD games that deride W:tA endlessly for that old stuff yet also cherry-pick which elements of, say, Mage, that they choose to talk about. Mage, with its beginnings every bit as sordid and ill-researched as early Werewolf material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T05:04:41-08:00","id":776520,"title":"","content":"Speak in whispers the WoD is one people will hear you and crash the thread. They will sing the praises of the ashtray known as Haight, as showing us the ONE TRUE WAY. Then proceed to explain that Garou in WoD is all about the insert splat here and how they must accept insert splat here while stating in the true believer voice that this is the only way to play.*<br /> <br /> *I am joking for the most part but subscribe to the belief that each game line stands alone. That the other splats are mere shadows in each other's worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T05:34:35-08:00","id":776525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=776520#post776520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *I am joking for the most part but subscribe to the belief that each game line stands alone. That the other splats are mere shadows in each other's worlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always thought that this was basically a copout and an excuse for lack of planning and design. The books aren't even written this way, even by writers and developers who might say the same thing you just said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T06:03:33-08:00","id":776532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=776525#post776525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always thought that this was basically a copout and an excuse for lack of planning and design. The books aren't even written this way, even by writers and developers who might say the same thing you just said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually if you only own one of the core books this is exactly how it is written. Look up any of the antagonists in the core book and you will see werewolves translated into that setting. These write ups are a shadow of the &quot;real&quot; splat. It is only when you have multiple core books that you start seeing the WoD as one. I write my chronicles in this pattern. The great thing about both CWoD and NWoD is the stories that you tell and if you want to write The WoD U.N. Chronicle: The search for Harmony great. If you want to play in WoD cross-over Mania that is awesome. I don't. I feel that each game line has a unique and interesting take on horror and tragedy and bringing in the other splats diminishes that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T07:43:31-08:00","id":776575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=776532#post776532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually if you only own one of the core books this is exactly how it is written. Look up any of the antagonists in the core book and you will see werewolves translated into that setting. These write ups are a shadow of the &quot;real&quot; splat. It is only when you have multiple core books that you start seeing the WoD as one. I write my chronicles in this pattern. The great thing about both CWoD and NWoD is the stories that you tell and if you want to write The WoD U.N. Chronicle: The search for Harmony great. If you want to play in WoD cross-over Mania that is awesome. I don't. I feel that each game line has a unique and interesting take on horror and tragedy and bringing in the other splats diminishes that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason the core books are written so lupines use disciplines or leeches use gifts is because they draw upon that corebook's rules for running those things. If you look at each line as a holistic entity, however, you will see that they are written more faithfully. For example, Pariah in Children of the Night is written using rules from a Werewolf supplement along with the actual Werewolf rules and with the relevant rules from Vampire. If the games were truly written as you claim they are, then Pariah would have been written entirely with Vampire rules and no reference back to abomination rules in Werewolf. For that matter, the abomination rules themselves contradict your claims.<br /> <br /> So the core books write up the various supernaturals in terms of the rules in that core book, but that doesn't mean that the different supernaturals are genuinely being treated as something different from their home lines. And the entire idea that each cWoD game is in its own little pocket universe is a terrible explanation for what amounted to poorly thought out game design (writing the games so that crossovers would be difficult to impossible) that was not supported in any given line's supplements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T09:11:37-08:00","id":776622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=776575#post776575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason the core books are written so lupines use disciplines or leeches use gifts is because they draw upon that corebook's rules for running those things. If you look at each line as a holistic entity, however, you will see that they are written more faithfully. For example, Pariah in Children of the Night is written using rules from a Werewolf supplement along with the actual Werewolf rules and with the relevant rules from Vampire. If the games were truly written as you claim they are, then Pariah would have been written entirely with Vampire rules and no reference back to abomination rules in Werewolf. For that matter, the abomination rules themselves contradict your claims.<br /> <br /> So the core books write up the various supernaturals in terms of the rules in that core book, but that doesn't mean that the different supernaturals are genuinely being treated as something different from their home lines. And the entire idea that each cWoD game is in its own little pocket universe is a terrible explanation for what amounted to poorly thought out game design (writing the games so that crossovers would be difficult to impossible) that was not supported in any given line's supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abominations yet another of 1st edition madness that plagued the game lines for years. You will notice that the only splat that even attempts to stick with something even vaguely resembling the original is Werewolf. Mages die and become the clan of the embrace. Fae die and become either Kiysad or the original embracing clan. The fact is if the WoD was unified as you have stated then Hunter the Reckoning instead of Foe books would have went with hey buy Vampire the Masquerade to make vampires. You want Werewolves pick up Apocalypse. At anytime after the 1st edition of Vampire was printed White Wolf could have said hey let's put Vampires from Masquerade into Werewolf and listed a brief summary of powers. The fact is they didn't. I can play Werewolf the Apocalypse and only Werewolf the Apocalypse without buying a single other line in the WoD. <br /> You will notice that none of the ToJ books linked into the others, beyond a brief mention here or there where it was thematic i.e. Garou and Corax outing Vampires in the Weaver Ascendant chapter. Yes certain writers or events crossed over in furthering the Meta plot of the various game lines. I don't think the writers were lazy, I think that fans wanted to be able to do crossovers and so every time that a writer tried it bit the game lines involved. <br /> We have different views and that is fine. I by no means think my way is the only way to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T15:52:00-08:00","id":776849,"title":"","content":"It's about winks and nods. But the games work best when they lie on their own merits. The problem that comes with shoving them together is that they trample each other thematically and cosmologically. It's a testament to their design that they offer such unique and different gaming experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T18:26:50-08:00","id":776919,"title":"","content":"In the end, though, that is such a taste question. I do crossover, but I wouldn't force anyone else to do it unless they wanted to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T22:40:16-08:00","id":777010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=776919#post776919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, though, that is such a taste question. I do crossover, but I wouldn't force anyone else to do it unless they wanted to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is a matter of taste, agreed; it is <i>not </i>a foregone conclusion.<br /> <br /> Back on topic, I think some of the best/worst things about 1st edition was the art. So gloriously dated and silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T19:22:05-08:00","id":777499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=777010#post777010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Back on topic, I think some of the best/worst things about 1st edition was the art. So gloriously dated and silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like you said, matter of taste. I loved 1st edition art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T01:47:28-08:00","id":777627,"title":"","content":"You will have to tell me which of these awesome pieces are your favourite. I have tons more! Thank the Gods that SCAR isn't doing Werewolf art anymore. The worst thing about early Werewolf was the overabunadance of SCAR work.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/2C1W8Hv.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/rlbRVyz.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/M2E8CpD.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T08:09:11-08:00","id":777767,"title":"","content":"Mmmm it is like tabasco sauce for the eyes. It burns so good. When WTF DnD over on Something Awful did their bit on Werewolf, they used a lot of early art and a lot of SCAR material. Understandably.<br /> <br /> There is no accounting for taste but by any technical standard that is<i> bad</i> art. Still love it though, it is sort of painfully iconic... almost a visual equivalent to the entire CoG tribebook. :P<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T14:21:47-08:00","id":777916,"title":"","content":"Was... that the only artist the folks developing Werewolf knew back in '93? Or maybe someone's cousin who really needed a job?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T00:34:18-08:00","id":778165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/773235-the-best-worst-1st-ed-messes-in-wta?p=777916#post777916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was... that the only artist the folks developing Werewolf knew back in '93? Or maybe someone's cousin who really needed a job?</div> </div> </div> </div>In their defense, early books have some Ron Spencer, Alex Sheikman, Richard Kane Ferguson and Josh Timbrook. There was also a number of &quot;in vogue&quot; current artists of the early 90s, whose work I've seen all over Cyberpunk 2020, Shadowrun and so on. Sadly, I'm assuming for the reason of &quot;We were young and needed money&quot; they gave out a ton of their art to SCAR studios. I'm assuming it's a similar reason for why Exalted 3 has some truly and utterly bad artwork as well.<br /> <br /> I wonder if Rich could give us some funny story about how it came to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","